dropped the body
type mismatch
--
N5008 [temp.class.spec.match] + [dcl.ref]/6: `function<R(ArgTypes...)>'
matched against `int(const int &)' deduces ArgTypes = {const int &}; the
element was bound in its parsed form (a frontend_pointer), so a template
parameter resolving to it (`T' of forward<const int &>) stayed unconverted
and `static_cast<T &&>(t)' saw `frontend_pointer &&' -- no reference
collapsing, "type mismatch on static_cast", and std::forward's body was
dropped for every std::function with a reference parameter (libstdc++
_Function_handler::_M_invoke).
